GOAL: Fix a bug in /gin/response_writer.go.

BUG: `responseWriter.WriteHeader(code int)` currently updates the recorded status even when the response has already been sent:

    func (w *responseWriter) WriteHeader(code int) {
        if code > 0 && w.status != code {
            if w.Written() {
                debugPrint("[WARNING] Headers were already written. Wanted to override status code %d with %d", w.status, code)
            }
            w.status = code
        }
    }

So after `w.WriteHeader(http.StatusOK); w.WriteHeaderNow()` (response already sent, client got 200), a later `w.WriteHeader(http.StatusUnauthorized)` makes `w.Status()` report 401 even though 401 was never sent to the client. Expected: once the response has been written, the recorded status must not change (the warning is logged and the call is ignored).

FIX: add an early `return` in the already-written branch, i.e.:

    func (w *responseWriter) WriteHeader(code int) {
        if code > 0 && w.status != code {
            if w.Written() {
                debugPrint("[WARNING] Headers were already written. Wanted to override status code %d with %d", w.status, code)
                return
            }
            w.status = code
        }
    }

Change ONLY that function in /gin/response_writer.go. Do not touch anything else. Do NOT edit or delete any pre-existing *_test.go file.

