BUG (panic in Context.NegotiateFormat): in /gin/context.go, NegotiateFormat does:

    for _, accepted := range c.Accepted {
        for _, offer := range offered {
            i := 0
            for ; i < len(accepted); i++ {
                if accepted[i] == '*' || offer[i] == '*' {
                    return offer
                }
                if accepted[i] != offer[i] {
                    break
                }
            }
            if i == len(accepted) {
                return offer
            }
        }
    }

When the Accept header value is longer than the offer (e.g. header "image/tiff-fx" with offer "image/tiff"), `offer[i]` indexes out of range -> `panic: runtime error: index out of range [10] with length 10`. Expected: no panic; the offer simply does not match, so NegotiateFormat returns "" (or a later matching offer).

FIX (minimal, in /gin/context.go only): guard the loop so it stops when the offer is exhausted, e.g.:

    i := 0
    for ; i < len(accepted) && i < len(offer); i++ {
        if accepted[i] == '*' || offer[i] == '*' {
            return offer
        }
        if accepted[i] != offer[i] {
            break
        }
    }
    if i == len(accepted) && i == len(offer) {
        return offer
    }

Careful: the pre-existing test `TestContextNegotiationFormat` expects `c.NegotiateFormat("*/*") == "*/*"` and `c.NegotiateFormat("text/*") == "text/*"` with Accept "text/html", and `NegotiateFormat(MIMEJSON) == ""` with Accept "text/html". Make sure those still pass: with accepted="text/html", offer="*/*": i=0 -> offer[0]=='*' -> return offer. Good. With accepted="text/html", offer="text/*": i=0..3 equal, i=4: accepted[4]=='/' vs offer[4]=='*' -> return offer. Good. With accepted="text/html", offer="application/json": i=0 mismatch -> break, i=0 != len(accepted) -> continue. Good. With accepted="text/html", offer="text/html": full match -> i==len(accepted)==len(offer) -> return. Good.

